    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                          VETO MESSAGE - No. 68\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7295, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\n      the filling of borrow pits in Jamaica Bay; and  to  amend  chapter\n      288  of  the  laws of 2014 amending the environmental conservation\n      law relating to the filling of borrow  pits  in  Jamaica  Bay,  in\n      relation to making the provisions of such chapter permanent\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would change the criteria for filling the Jamaica Bay borrow\npits  to  comply  with  federal Ocean Dumping Act criteria for the unre-\nstricted ocean dumping of dredged material, which is not  applicable  to\nJamaica Bay.\n\n  I  vetoed  an  identical  bill  last  year because the more costly and\nrestrictive standards required under the bill would threaten the  resto-\nration of Jamaica Bay without any appreciable improvement in water qual-\nity  protection.  The Department of Environmental Conservation (DEC) may\nonly grant a permit allowing fill material to be placed in  the  Jamaica\nBay  borrow pits if the sediments are Class A material, where laboratory\ntesting has confirmed there will be no toxicity to aquatic life.  Pursu-\nant to Environmental Conservation Law Section 15-0505, there is current-\nly  a  five-year  moratorium  in  place  on  the use of other classes of\ndredged materials for this purpose that is set to  expire  on  June  30,\n2022.\n \n  While  the goal of this bill is laudable, the classification currently\nused by DEC achieves the same level of protection as the  federal  ocean\ndumping  criteria.  By  imposing new standards and testing methods, this\nbill would significantly increase the  cost  and  thereby  decrease  the\navailability  of  fill materials. Millions of yards of fill material are\nneeded to restore the borrow pits.  This  bill  would  imperil  critical\nefforts  in  the restoration of Jamaica Bay and unnecessarily delay this\nimportant work. For these reasons, I am constrained to  veto  this  bill\nagain.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
